--TEST--
A capture reaches the program as the value the match already converted, so `Core\Router\Match::params` answers a union and not one text type — `rule:routing/matched-once-before-the-handler` and `rule:routing/a-capture-narrows-to-a-closed-set`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A bound stated as a type. § 1 has the server compute "typed parameters", so a
// `{id: uint}` capture arrives as the number the match converted rather than as
// digits the handler would parse a second time -- and two parsers of one
// segment is the shape that can disagree. `Core\Router\Match` therefore answers
// one member per conversion the matcher performs, and a `tainted string`
// binding -- exactly right for the text arm and for that arm alone -- refuses
// every other. § 5's `decimal` and `Core\Uuid` are in that union because their
// readers are reachable from the walk; a `bool` is not and arrives on the text
// arm. An enum needs no member -- a case is its backing integer, converted.
//
// The mark sits on the text arm because a segment is a piece of the request
// path the peer wrote. The two numeric arms carry none: a converted `int` has
// no spelling an injection could survive, which is why the qualifier axes are
// defined over `string` and `bytes` and not over every type.
var $matched = Core\Request::route();
if ($matched != null) {
    foreach ($matched->params() as tainted string $capture) {
    }
    echo $matched->name() ?? "none", "\n";
    echo $matched->param("id") ?? "none", "\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `tainted string`, found `uint|int|decimal|tainted string|Core\Uuid|Parses`
   --> case.nvs:18:36
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
